<title>BELGIUM: EU agrees to start 1997/98 sugar exports on Aug 6.</title>
<headline>EU agrees to start 1997/98 sugar exports on Aug 6.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union agreed on Wednesday to hold the first 1997/98 (July/June) white sugar export tender on August 6, European Commission officials said.</p>
<p>They said the sugar management committee also decided to close 1996/97 sugar export tenders on July 30.</p>
<p>For the past two seasons, the EU has launched new export tenders in August, one month later than usual, reflecting a slower pace in achieving the export target.</p>
<p>As in previous years, EU export refunds for the remainder of July will be based on a split between the Paris August and October futures contracts.</p>
<p>The Paris August contract expires on Friday.</p>
<p>The average difference between the last five closing prices of the two contracts is added to the October futures prices and the total used as a basis for calculating the export refund.</p>
</text>
